        "original_id": "040ea420-9d90-584f-8983-572b844aa8e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downtown East, Minneapolis; downtown Minneapolis; North Loop district; Minneapolis, Minnesota\n- Organizations: Minnesota Twins; Minnesota Fighting Saints; Calgary Cowboys; Birmingham Bulls; World Hockey Association\n- Products: Target Field; Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome\n- People: Pat Westrum\n- Topics: 2009 Minnesota Twins season\n\nFacts:\n- Pat Westrum was born on March 3, 1948, in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- Pat Westrum played 237 regular season games in the World Hockey Association between 1974 and 1978.\n- Pat Westrum played for the Minnesota Fighting Saints, Calgary Cowboys, and Birmingham Bulls.\n- The 2009 Minnesota Twins season was the team's final season at the Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome.\n- Target Field opened in 2010 as the new stadium for the Minnesota Twins.\n- The Minnesota Twins moved into Target Field at the start of the 2010 season.\n- Target Field is a baseball park in the historic warehouse, or North Loop, district of downtown Minneapolis.",
